### ✅ **2. Dodanie bloku odbijającego neutrony przy zasilaniu redstonem**
Stwórz nowy blok `NEUTRON_SHOOTER_BLOCK` z logiką redstonową i odbijaniem neutronów:

```java
public class NeutronShooterBlock extends Block {
    public NeutronShooterBlock(Properties properties) {
        super(properties);
    }

    @Override
    public BlockEntity newBlockEntity(BlockPos pos, BlockState state) {
        return new NeutronShooterBlockEntity(pos, state);
    }
}
```

**Klasa `NeutronShooterBlockEntity`:**
```java
public class NeutronShooterBlockEntity extends BlockEntity {
    private boolean isPowered = false;
    private int cooldown = 0;

    public NeutronShooterBlockEntity(BlockPos pos, BlockState state) {
        super(ModBlockEntities.NEUTRON_SHOOTER.get(), pos, state);
    }

    public void setPowered(boolean powered) {
        this.isPowered = powered;
    }

    public boolean isPowered() {
        return isPowered;
    }

    public void tick(Level level, BlockPos pos, BlockState state, NeutronShooterBlockEntity entity) {
        if (isPowered && cooldown <= 0) {
            // Wystrzeliwanie neutronów
            Vec3 velocity = new Vec3(0, 0, -1); // Kierunek (np. w stronę gracza)
            level.addFreshEntity(new NuclearParticle(
                NuclearParticle.Type.NEUTRON,
                pos,
                velocity,
                20 // Czas życia cząstki
            ));
            cooldown = 20; //Cooldown
        } else if (cooldown > 0) {
            cooldown--;
        }
    }
}
```

**Zarejestruj blok i blok entity w `ModBlockEntities`:**
